  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_win",
  "prompt": "Joost, the pricing lead, is choosing the products for a weekly competitor price watch in the second half of 2025 and asks for the best sellers of each category in the first half. Take the orders with an order_ts from 2025-01-01 00:00:00 up to but not including 2025-07-01 00:00:00; order_ts holds UTC time. A product's net revenue is the sum of quantity times unit_price_eur minus line_discount_eur over its lines in those orders, and only products with at least one such line count. Within each category, place the products from the highest net revenue down. When products tie on net revenue, the lower product_id comes first. Keep exactly the first 3 places of each category, or every product when a category has fewer than 3. Return one row for each product kept, with five columns, in this order: category_name; product_id; net_revenue_eur, not rounded; revenue_rank, the product's place in its category, from 1 to 3; and category_share_pct, 100 times the product's net revenue divided by the net revenue of all the products of its category, rounded to 1 decimal. Sort by category_name from A to Z, then by net_revenue_eur from high to low, then by product_id from low to high.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "category_name",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "product_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
